Id: ldap001w
Severity: WARN
Category: accounts
Check: check_ldap
References: slapd.conf(5), ldap.conf(5)
Controls: CIS 3.3, 5.2; NIST AC-3, IA-5(7); ISO 5.17, 8.3; CE User access control

An LDAP config file holds a credential and anyone can read it: a
client's bind password, or the directory manager's password. Whoever
copies it binds as the service, or owns the directory. Leave such
files readable by root alone.
